    "https://www.trine.edu/career-services/employers.aspx": {
      "title": "Employers' guide to recruiting students and alumni",
      "description": "Recruiting Students and Alumni | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Career Center Employers Employers' guide to recruiting students and alumni More in this Page Career Center Contact Career Services Employers Career Events Handshake Complete the Graduate Survey Intern/Co-Op/Experiential Learning Survey Internships and Co-ops Student Resources Resume / Cover Letter Graduate School Personal Statements Career Exploration Job Search Tools Interviewing Networking Professional Image and Etiquette Career Readiness Leadership Development Programs Quinncia - Resume Assistance Recruiting Students and Alumni The Trine Career Center encourages employers to to recruit and engage in on-campus\n                                    activities as well as inviting students to your facility to develop future opportunities. Convenient, full-service, on-campus recruiting. Introductions to faculty and relevant student organizations. Advertise positions through multi-channel marketing such as Handshake, campus monitors\n                                       and faculty announcements Create opportunities to meet students through on-campus events- Your way! Sponsor career fairs and other events for added visibility Employer of the Day Recruiting Table Trine offers employers, graduate programs, and other organizations the opportunity\n                                       to reserve a spot in the University Center to engage with students. This can serve\n                                       as either a networking or recruiting session, with exclusive access for your organization. Currently, there are no limitations on the number of days available for reservation,\n                                       and there is no associated cost. We've scheduled these sessions from 11:00 AM to 2:00\n                                       PM, considering it the optimal time for student traffic and exposure. You have the flexibility to design your own marketing materials, which we will distribute\n                                    to students and display on the monitor. Please ensure that the file dimensions are\n                                    1920x1080 pixels. Kindly submit your marketing material at least 24 hours before your\n                                    scheduled session to netcherc@trine.edu . For any further inquiries, please contact millera1@trine.edu . To secure your preferred date, please utilize the following registration link: Register Now Thank you for considering Trine University as part of your recruitment strategy. We\n                                       look forward to collaborating with you. Handshake is a fast, powerful early career recruiting platform for hiring Trine students\n                                       and alumni. Consistent with the NACE Principles for Professional Conduct , all job postings must contain accurate information about the organization offering\n                                    employment and the position offered, and all employers must comply with all Equal\n                                    Employment Opportunity standards. *Trine University reserves the right to decline postings and recruitment for positions\n                                          that require a financial investment by Trine students or alumni, or postings or recruitment\n                                          for positions that conflict with the NACE Principles for Professional Conduct . For upcoming events, please visit the Career Events page . Please contact us for questions or assistance. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/great-place-to-work.aspx": {
      "title": "Trine University",
      "description": "Trine University - a great place to work! Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Great place to work Trine University More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! A great place to work! As a faculty or staff member at Trine, you will be a part of an institution that: is ranked among the best regional universities in the Midwest by U.S. News and World Report and Princeton Review has more than 99% of graduates employed or in graduate school within six months of\n                                       graduation offers students personal interaction with an average class size of 19.7 and the opportunity\n                                       to work on real-world projects through Innovation One offers competitive salary and benefits has invested more than $176 million in campus improvements since 2000 In addition, you’ll find great quality of life in the area around Trine University\n                                    along with year-round recreational opportunities, including: affordable cost of living below state and national averages the state’s largest collection of lakes (along with Indiana’s only toboggan slide ) four school corporations serving Steuben County art galleries and attractions, annual festivals and celebrations easy access to Fort Wayne – Indiana’s second-largest city -- 35 miles away via interstate major metropolitan areas such as Cleveland, Detroit, Chicago and Indianapolis about\n                                       three hours away via interstate Watch other community videos Opens in new window To learn more about the amenities in and around Angola and Steuben County, check out\n                                    the following websites: City of Angola Opens in new window Angola Chamber of Commerce Opens in new window Steuben County Metropolitan School District of Steuben County Opens in new window Fremont Community Schools Opens in new window Hamilton Community Schools Prairie Heights Community Schools Opens in new window Visit Northern Indiana Lakes County Opens in new window Steuben County Economic Development Corporation Visit Fort Wayne Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/administrative-assistant-chem-design.aspx": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Administrative Assistant Administrative Assistant More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Administrative Assistant Angola, Indiana Summary Provides support to managers at the Chair level or faculty in the department.  Performs\n                                    diversified and confidential secretarial and administrative duties requiring experience,\n                                    skill, and knowledge of organization policies and practices. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Manage travel schedule, plans and expense reports in a timely manner. Prepare complex presentations with graphics, other documents, and reports. Organize and update files, reference materials, and confidential / proprietary business\n                                       information, removing outdated items. Screen and prioritize appointments, calls, and respond to inquiries from internal/external\n                                       sources. Initiate routine and some non-routine correspondence with minimal direction. Pay invoices, track expenses, and maintain departmental budget. Assists and tracks all budget/requisitions and travel forms. Takes meeting notes at department meetings and distributes to faculty. Plans and coordinates departmental receptions and functions. Assists students when appropriate. Maintains office supplies. Assist in maintaining lab supplies and ordering supplies. Distributes department mail. Assists in the general upkeep of the department, including display cases and bulletin\n                                       boards. Maintains web profile for school and department Performs Accepts Analysis for ASOEC All other duties as assigned Education and/or Experience A minimum high school or GED diploma and a minimum of 1-2 years of business administration\n                                    experience. Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/assistant-coach-skating.aspx": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Coach | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Assistant Coach Assistant Coach More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Assistant Figure & Synchronized Skating Coach Angola, Indiana Summary: The Assistant Figure and Synchronized Skating Coach supports the overall growth and\n                                       advancement of Trine University's Varsity Figure and Synchronized Skating teams. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Be a hands-on coach and assist with practice plans and running practices for both\n                                       figure and synchronized skating. Assist with choreography, skills lessons and off-ice\n                                       training. Assist with providing a seamless Game Day experience by coordinating lodging, travel,\n                                       meals, and assist with team management at competition. Assist with auditions, summer fitness, required pre-season documentation and overall\n                                       program development. Actively involved with music selection, program concept development,\n                                       dress designs, off-season training, and identifying goals for the upcoming season. Play a key role in on-boarding and retaining skaters by engaging with prospective student-athletes,\n                                       supporting current Trine skaters, attending off-campus recruiting events and assisting\n                                       with on-campus preview days and skating camps. Be team-oriented and assist with other duties as necessary including game management,\n                                       team bonding, study tables, and volunteer events. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree, USFS, and PSA Memberships, Liability Insurance, and SafeSport Certification. Some experience with skill instruction, practice planning, competition day duties\n                                          and administrative responsibilities relating to figure and synchronized skating. Proficient in basic computer skills. Desired Qualifications Ideal candidate will have direct experience with skill, instruction, planning practices,\n                                                assisting with competition day duties and administrative responsibilities in relation\n                                                to figure and/or synchronized skating. Ideal candidate will have competitive experience including national /  international\n                                                competitions and/or have coached a skater or team at the national  / international\n                                                level. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/campus-safety-officer.aspx": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Campus Safety Officer Campus Safety Officer More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Campus Safety Officer Angola, Indiana Summary The Campus Safety Officer is responsible for the safety and security of students,\n                                    visitors, and employees, as well as the safety and security of the facilities.  The\n                                    Campus Safety Officer supports the needs of our students by being available and responsive.  \n                                    The Campus Safety Officer must be customer service-oriented, maintain a professional\n                                    appearance, and maintain professional relationships with local authorities. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Assisting students, visitors, and staff in accordance with Trine University guidelines. Inform and educate students, visitors, and staff within the Trine University guidelines. Proactively patrol, as a deterrent to criminal activity or violations of Trine University\n                                       rules. Maintain high visibility during patrol. Look for any hazards to the safety and well-being of students, visitors or staff. Maintain sound public relations, in an effort to support and promote Trine University. Report and document accidents, incidents, and disciplinary issues as required. Cooperate with law enforcement authorities per Trine University guidelines. Carry out other duties, tasks, and responsibilities as may be assigned or directed\n                                       by the Dean of Students. Education and/or Experience High School Diploma or General Education Degree required.  One to two years of related\n                                    experience/training required. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Apply Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for employment without\n                                       regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic information,\n                                       citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by law, unless\n                                       such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will comply with\n                                       its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals\n                                       with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/dir-development.aspx": {
      "title": "Director Development",
      "description": "Director Development | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Director Development Director Development More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Director of Development Angola, Indiana Summary Trine University is seeking an experienced front-line fundraiser. The Director of\n                                    Development shall formulate, implement and oversee a strategic fundraising plan designed\n                                    to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major gift prospects, as well as current\n                                    and past donors for the purpose of providing financial support for the priorities\n                                    of the University. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Plan, develop, implement, administer, evaluate, and monitor an aggressive major gift\n                                       fundraising program in an assigned geographical area and/or by a determined portfolio\n                                       of individuals, businesses, and corporations. Solicit gifts of $10,000 and above (annual, major, planned) from alumni and friends\n                                       of the University, with a particular emphasis on identified campaign priorities. Support the President, Vice President for Advancement, and other Advancement staff\n                                       in collaboration and strategy for direct research and preparation of briefing materials,\n                                       talking points, and meeting strategies. As appropriate, facilitate interaction with\n                                       principal prospects by the President and VP. Conduct appropriate fundraising activities in support of the budget and programs focused\n                                       on individual/corporate donor upgrading, cultivation, and solicitation. Cultivate and steward present donors as well as complete discovery visits with new\n                                       potential donors. Produce well-written, accurate, and timely follow-up and related correspondence such\n                                       as comprehensive proposals, related budgets, contact reports, thank you letters, emails,\n                                       and calls in support of cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding prospects. Maintain donor/prospect record-keeping system, ensuring that accurate and complete\n                                       records of information and activity are prepared and maintained in the data management\n                                       system. Requires flexible scheduling, significant time away from the office to meet with prospective\n                                       donors, whether local, regional, or national, as assigned, periodic weekend and evening\n                                       assignments, as well as activities and other duties as assigned. Coordinate priorities for all proposals with the Assistant Vice President for Advancement\n                                       and the Vice President for Advancement. Additional related duties as assigned. Requirements At least 2-3 years of experience of fundraising experience Experience in planned giving is preferred but not required Bachelor’s degree required Overnight travel is required Driver’s license is required Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Benefits offered include: Health – medical, dental, vision, prescription drugs, flex spending or HSA accounts Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for employer contribution\n                                       of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with employee\n                                       life insurance (1½ times annual salary) Education – after 6 months of full-time service education benefits are available for\n                                       employee, spouse, and dependent children Vacation and Sick Pay – in accordance with Trine's policy Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/dir-dual-enrollment.aspx": {
      "title": "Director of Dual Enrollment",
      "description": "Director of Dual Enrollment Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Director of Dual Enrollment Director of Dual Enrollment More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Director of Dual Enrollment Angola, Indiana Full-time Summary Under the direction of the Vice President for Enrollment Management (VPEM), the Director\n                                    of Dual Enrollment serves as the administrative leader of Trine University's Dual\n                                    Enrollment Program. This position is responsible for the strategic planning, growth,\n                                    administration, compliance, and assessment of all dual enrollment initiatives, including\n                                    on-campus dual enrollment, high school partnerships, online offerings, homeschool\n                                    partnerships, and other early college opportunities. The Director develops and implements strategies to expand access to dual enrollment\n                                    opportunities while ensuring academic quality, regulatory compliance, and a positive\n                                    student experience. This position serves as the primary liaison between Trine University\n                                    and partnering schools, academic departments, faculty liaisons, and community stakeholders. The Director of Dual Enrollment provides leadership in identifying and cultivating\n                                    new partnerships, overseeing accreditation and compliance processes, supporting faculty\n                                    and instructors, and advancing the University's enrollment and academic goals. The\n                                    successful candidate must possess strong leadership, communication, organizational,\n                                    and relationship-building skills, along with the ability to think strategically and\n                                    manage multiple priorities. Travel throughout Indiana and surrounding regions is required. Duties and Responsibilities Leadership and Strategic Planning Provide leadership and supervision for the Dual Enrollment team. Develop, implement, and assess short-term and long-term strategic plans for dual enrollment\n                                       growth and student success. Develop and implement strategies to increase the matriculation of dual enrollment\n                                       students into Trine University undergraduate programs, including communication plans,\n                                       enrollment pathways, and transition initiatives Establish annual goals, key performance indicators, and assessment measures for dual\n                                       enrollment programs. Collaborate with academic leadership to identify opportunities for new dual enrollment\n                                       pathways, certificates, and academic partnerships. Partnership Development and Outreach Cultivate, develop, and maintain relationships with high schools, career centers,\n                                       homeschool organizations, and other educational partners. Identify and pursue opportunities to expand dual enrollment offerings and geographic\n                                       reach. Represent Trine University at school meetings, conferences, professional organizations,\n                                       and community events. Market dual enrollment and early college opportunities to students, parents, counselors,\n                                       teachers, and school administrators. Academic Quality and Compliance Serve as the institutional lead for NACEP accreditation and applicable State of Indiana\n                                       dual credit requirements. Oversee faculty liaison activities and coordinate regular meetings with faculty liaisons. Lead the review and approval process for new dual enrollment instructors in collaboration\n                                       with academic departments and faculty liaisons. Assist with professional development opportunities for dual enrollment instructors. Conduct classroom observations and program reviews to evaluate instructional quality,\n                                       course rigor, student engagement, and compliance with university standards. Manage and maintain the Dual Enrollment Student Handbook and Faculty Liaison Handbook. Operations and Student Support Oversee communication and marketing plans for dual enrollment students, families,\n                                       instructors, and school partners. Provide exceptional customer service and support to students, parents, instructors,\n                                       and school personnel. Manage processes related to course scheduling, curriculum coordination, conflict resolution,\n                                       and program operations. Oversee dual enrollment course listings, web content, and program information to ensure\n                                       accuracy and accessibility. Support enrollment operations during peak periods, including student processing, Slate\n                                       management, registration activities, and payment coordination. Assist team members with day-to-day operations as needed to ensure efficient program\n                                       delivery. Additional Responsibilities Attend school recognition events and present honor cords and awards on behalf of the\n                                       University. Prepare reports and analyses related to program growth, enrollment trends, student\n                                       success, and partnership effectiveness. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university, a Master’s degree in education\n                                    or a business-related field, and three or more years of successful admission or related\n                                    experience and/or training; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Salary Competitive based on experience. Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid vacation and sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\n                                    Candidates should send a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, detailing all academic\n                                    & professional experience, plus the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three\n                                    references within their application. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/financial-aid-counselor.aspx": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor| Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Financial Aid Counselor Financial Aid Counselor More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Financial Aid Counselor Angola, Indiana Summary The Financial Aid Counselor reports directly to the Director of Financial Aid and\n                                    will assist in all areas of financial aid, including Title IV programs (Direct Loans,\n                                    Pell, TEACH etc.), State Grants, institutional programs, and all other aid as it relates\n                                    to the financial aid program. The Financial Aid Counselor also handles day-to-day\n                                    operations of the Office of Financial Aid that are outlined below. Essential Duties and Responsibilities The Financial Aid Counselor works and contributes through a team-oriented approach\n                                    to collaborate with the Director of Financial Aid in the overall planning and operations\n                                    of Trine’s financial aid programs, including Financial Aid Planning, application and\n                                    FAFSA processing, advising, policy and communication development, all direct and private\n                                    loan counseling, processing of private student loan applications, new and current\n                                    student packaging and any other functions deemed necessary to the department. The\n                                    Financial Aid Counselor handles day-to-day operations within the office to include\n                                    reporting to COD, daily ISIR Processing, Title IV Grant programs, and the DL Program.\n                                    In addition to these responsibilities, the Counselor will work collaboratively with\n                                    all areas within the University to enhance and support the financial aid programs;\n                                    and assist the Director in planning, implementation, and evaluation of all programs\n                                    and efforts. Evening hours and weekends may be required as needed, but are minimal.\n                                    Other duties as assigned by the Director are not limited to the following: Counsel students and their families on financial aid processes and procedures, including\n                                       making presentations for orientations, open houses, campus visits etc. Familiarity, assessment, compliance, and communication to the appropriate University\n                                       officers of federal and state financial aid compliance-related issues/policies. Financial Aid packaging to include – Verifications, Loan Certifications, Revisions\n                                       and all other packaging processes related to Financial Aid Ensure federal & state guidelines for student enrollment and financial aid eligibility\n                                       are met Assist with review process for Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) at the end of\n                                       every academic term Perform student “Needs Analysis” Review student files to ensure accurate funding Counsel students to determine financial aid needs /options Ensure compliance with federal & state policies Interact with outside agencies including the DOE and loan processing companies Inventory of materials and print pieces Website review and maintenance Provide direct customer support by routinely visiting with students during new student\n                                       orientation and preview days and any other times that a student needs financial assistance. Answer questions as they arise from students and their families about the financial\n                                       aid process by phone call, email or in person Keep students engaged with the University and supports retention, communication, and\n                                       academic rehabilitation. Perform other duties as assigned Education/Experience Prefer Bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university, and two or more years\n                                    of successful financial aid/advising or related experience and/or training; or equivalent\n                                    combination of education and experience. Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Benefits offered include: Health – medical, dental, vision, prescription drugs, flex spending or HSA accounts Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for employer contribution\n                                       of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with employee\n                                       life insurance (1½ times annual salary) Education – after 6 months of full-time service, education benefits are available\n                                       for employee, spouse, and dependent children Vacation and Sick Pay – in accordance with Trine's policy Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/housekeeper.aspx": {
      "title": "Housekeeper",
      "description": "Housekeeper | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers housekeeper Housekeeper More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Housekeeper Angola, Indiana Summary Trine University is seeking full-time 1st and 3rd shift housekeepers who will be responsible\n                                    for cleaning and maintaining University buildings and assisting with the setting up\n                                    of summer camps held on the Trine University campus. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Include, but are not limited to: Sweeping, mopping, scrubbing, striping and waxing of floors Washing windows and window sills Select, measure and mix products for cleaning jobs Clean, sanitize and polish restrooms and their fixtures Clean and polish classroom and office furniture Remove waste and debris Replace light bulbs and clean fixtures Set up tables and chairs for special events Stock closets with cleaning and paper products Sweep and shovel walkways 10' from all entrances. Education and/or Experience A High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED) is required. Job Requirements Willingness to perform duties associated with commercial cleaning, including operating\n                                    industrial-type cleaning equipment such as high-speed buffers, scrubbers, and carpet\n                                    cleaners; cleaning restrooms; moving heavy items such as tables and chairs and caring\n                                    for all responsible equipment. To perform this job successfully, an individual must\n                                    be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below\n                                    are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations\n                                    may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work Environment : While performing the essential functions of this job an employee is occasionally\n                                          exposed to wet, and/or humid conditions; high, precarious places; fumes and/or airborne\n                                          particles; toxic or caustic chemicals; outside weather conditions and vibration. The\n                                          noise level in the work environment is usually moderate. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations : Must maintain a valid driver's license. Physical Demands : The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met\n                                          by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While\n                                          performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand; walk;\n                                          use hands and arms; climb and balance on ladders; stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl; see,\n                                          talk, hear and smell. The employee must be able to lift and/or move up to 50 pounds\n                                          and strong enough to operate industrial-type cleaning equipment. Language Skills : Ability to read and interpret documents such as safety rules, product label instructions,\n                                          operating and maintenance instructions and procedure manuals. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Are you ready to join Trine? Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/human-resource-specialist.aspx": {
      "title": "Human Resource Specialist",
      "description": "Human Resource Specialist | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Human Resource Specialist Human Resource Specialist More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Human Resource Specialist Angola, Indiana Summary The Human Resources Specialist position is an integral member of the Human Resources\n                                       team. The Human Resources Specialist provides administrative support to the Office\n                                       of Human Resources on all personnel matters and human resources functions as needed.\n                                       Under the direction of the Director of Human Resources, this position will be responsible\n                                       for the onboarding of student workers, adjunct professors, and all other part-time\n                                       employees. In addition, assist the Director of Human Resources with performing a variety\n                                       of human resources operations and system activities. The Human Resource Specialist\n                                       primarily reports to the Director of Human Resources but may also take direction from\n                                       the Assistant Vice President for Human Resources. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Oversight of student hires, adjunct professors, and part-time employee onboarding\n                                       by conducting I9 verifications, new hire onboarding within ADP, and working with supervisors\n                                       and Financial Aid to ensure proper department allocations. Responsible for creating and maintaining personnel files in accordance with the University’s\n                                       established records retention guidelines. Enroll all CGPS adjunct professors in required training; ensuring completion or rescheduling\n                                       as necessary. Completes the IT New Hire request form for all CGPS adjunct professors. Oversight of student, adjunct professors, and part-time employee terminations within\n                                       the HRIS. Assist the Director of Human Resources with employee inquiries, employee communications,\n                                       and with special projects as needed. Completes monthly audit of new hire information with ADP and submits completed audit\n                                       to the Director of Human Resources. Completes monthly benefit invoice reconciliation and submits discrepancies with carriers,\n                                       makes appropriate updates within ADP.  Provides reconciled invoices to the Business\n                                       Office on a monthly basis. Completes employment verifications and unemployment requests for information Assist with the creation, distribution and tracking of ADA, FMLA and Non-FMLA leave\n                                       documentation/communication in accordance with federal and state regulations and University\n                                       policy. Seek approval for FMLA/ADA requests form the Director of Human Resources and/or\n                                       Assistance Vice President for HR. Assist with ensuring SIT and SUI state tax IDs are accurately maintained within ADP Assist with the preparation and scheduling of performance review forms. Assist with the scheduling and administration of University training programs. Other duties as assigned Education and/or Experience Bachelor's degree in Human Resources and/or equivalent experience. One to three years’ experience in Human Resources Experience with ADP Workforce Now preferred General knowledge of laws and regulations relating to recruiting, hiring and benefit\n                                             administration preferred. Excellent communication skills – verbal and writing Proficient in Microsoft Office Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Outstanding Benefits: Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health - medical, dental, flex spending, HSA accounts Life insurance - a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1 ½ times annual salary Paid vacation and sick time Retirement - after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Are you ready to join Trine? Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/instructional-support-assistant.aspx": {
      "title": "Instructional Support Assistant",
      "description": "Instructional Support Assistant | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Instructional Support Assistant Instructional Support Assistant More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Instructional Support Assistant Angola, Indiana Summary The Instructional Support Assistant collaborates with the online course development\n                                       team to complete administrative and instructional design initiatives. The role requires\n                                       coordination with the team to maintain quality and efficiency. This individual is\n                                       highly organized, detail-oriented, with strong writing and editing skills. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Align course content to established templates and standards. Review course content for consistent formatting, clarity, and grammar. Set up learning tools and provide instructions for users. Test course activities, links, and learning tools to ensure proper functionality. Resolve course issues that may create barriers for faculty or students. Verify course materials for accuracy and accessibility. Organize course files and resources to support efficient course development. Assist with training and documentation used in the course development process. Work with team members to meet deadlines and contribute to course quality initiatives. Additional duties as assigned. Education and/or Experience High school diploma and highly proficient computer skills required; bachelor's degree\n                                       preferred. Salary The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer.  Applicants are considered for\n                                       employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national\n                                       origin, genetic information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis\n                                       prohibited by law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. \n                                       Trine will comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to\n                                       qualified individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/maintenance.aspx": {
      "title": "Maintenance/Building Technician",
      "description": "Maintenance/Building Technician | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Maintenance/Building Technician Maintenance/Building Technician More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Maintenance/Building Mechanic Angola, Indiana Summary Maintenance assigned areas of facility by performing general maintenance, inspections,\n                                       and repair of the facility's buildings, electric and mechanical equipment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Duties include, but are not limited to, the following. Other duties may be assigned. Performs safety inspections of the facility’s fire extinguishers, exit signs/lights,\n                                       and emergency lights. Performs safety inspections and repairs of buildings and grounds of site Performs security inspections and repairs of exterior doors and windows Monitors daily operation of heating and domestic hot water boilers Performs minor repairs on electrical, mechanical, and plumbing systems (ballast replacements,\n                                       switch replacement, filter replacement, unplugs sinks and stools, etc.) Performs minor repairs to interior and exterior finishes (ceiling tile, floor tile,\n                                       carpet, painting, glass, cabinets, chalkboards, bookshelves, bulletin boards, walls,\n                                       doors, railings and partitions, etc.) Performs inspections and minor repairs to exterior (roof, roof drains, downspouts,\n                                       etc.) Performs preventive maintenance tasks for electrical, HVAC, and plumbing systems Completes and submits the required paperwork (timesheets, work orders, material slips,\n                                       etc.) Communicates effectively with site resident director/building administrator, housekeeping,\n                                       and Director of Campus Operations Communicates and reviews short- and long-term needs of site to Director of Campus\n                                       Operations Orders necessary maintenance materials and supplies Assists with campus snow removal to keep a safe environment. Education and/or Experience A High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED) is required. Job Requirements High School diploma or General Education Degree (GED), and a minimum of five years\n                                    of building maintenance or construction-related experience. Ability to read and interpret\n                                    blueprints. Outstanding Benefits Trine University offers a comprehensive benefit package designed to provide a variety\n                                    of choices to best fit your needs and the needs of your family. Some benefits offered\n                                    include: Health – medical, dental, vision, flex spending, HSA accounts Life Insurance – a variety of voluntary life options are available along with an employer\n                                       paid employee life policy valued at 1½ times annual salary Financial Insurance – employer paid Long Term Disability and voluntary Short-Term\n                                       Disability, Accident, Hospital Indemnity, and Critical Illness options are available Paid vacation and sick time Retirement – after one year of full-time service you are eligible for an employer\n                                       contribution of 5% and up to an additional 5% employer match Education – after 6 months of full-time service, undergraduate education benefits\n                                       are available for employee, spouse, and dependent children Are you ready to join Trine? Opens in new window Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply to this program Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
