    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-chemistry.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct in Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct - Chemistry | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Chemistry Adjunct in Chemistry More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Chemistry Lab Angola, Indiana Summary Teaching responsibilities will focus on general chemistry.  Salary is based on the\n                                    number of credit hours taught. Candidates must have earned a Bachelor's Degree in Chemistry with teaching experience\n                                    preferred. The Department of Science at Trine University is a part of the Rinker-Ross School\n                                    of Health Sciences, and offers B.S degrees in chemistry, biochemistry, biology, and\n                                    forensic science.  The department is housed in the Best Hall of Science and has recently\n                                    moved into a new $6.6 million, 26,000 square-foot addition.  The addition includes\n                                    new biochemistry, organic, and physical/inorganic chemistry laboratories as well as\n                                    space for student research.  The department is well equipped with modern instrumentation\n                                    for both teaching and research, with significant additions including: three GCs, GCMS,\n                                    HPLC, microwave plasma spectrometer, FTIR, and NMR (60 MHz) with multi-element probe,\n                                    having been made within the last five years. Applicants should send a detailed CV, a letter describing their qualifications for\n                                    teaching laboratories and copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Required Education Candidates must have teaching experience and have completed graduate work in chemistry. Salary Salary is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/adjunct-criminal-justice.aspx": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor -  Criminal Justice | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Adjunct Professor -  Criminal Justice Adjunct Professor -  Criminal Justice More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Adjunct Professor - Criminal Justice Angola, Indiana Summary: The Criminal Justice Department is now accepting applications for a part-time position\n                                    teaching on the main campus in Angola, Indiana.  Teaching responsibilities will focus\n                                    on 1 or 2 sections of Criminal Law and Criminal Procedure and special topics in the\n                                    criminal justice field. This position requires in-person instruction located at Trine University’s main campus\n                                    in Angola, Indiana. We accept applications for this part-time role year-round. Applicants will be reviewed\n                                       and contacted as openings become available. Education and Experience Candidates must have at a minimum a Master’s degree in Criminal Justice or in a closely\n                                    related field. Salary Salary is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                       without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                       information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                       law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                       comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                       individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
