      "title": "Undergraduate Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Hybrid Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Hybrid Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Hybrid More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Hybrid Detroit, Michigan Summary Trine University invites applications for part-time adjunct positions. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to support program and enrollment growth.\n                                    Applications are active for one year from submission date. This adjunct faculty position\n                                    is for online faculty who will travel to our Detroit, Michigan location oncer per\n                                    eight week term, per course (this is subject to change). The Adjunct Faculty Role The University’s mission is to promote intellectual and personal development through\n                                    personally focused learning opportunities, preparing students to succeed, lead and\n                                    serve. Our faculty are responsible for ensuring students are successful in the online\n                                    classroom and are prepared for the complexities of today’s workplace. It is expected that adjunct faculty will: Actively engage students through frequent interaction and convey a genuine enthusiasm\n                                       for their learning. Provide thorough and constructive feedback, utilizing rubrics to effectively assess\n                                       learners’ work, while also acknowledging learner accomplishments. Demonstrate relevant and current subject-matter expertise and help students connect\n                                       concepts across their academic program. Work effectively with the TrineOnline team to seek continuous improvement for all\n                                       TrineOnline courses and programs. Adjunct Faculty Training All new faculty teaching online are required to successfully complete onboarding training\n                                    as a condition of hire. Required Education A terminal degree from an accredited institution of higher learning with a minimum\n                                       of 18 graduate credit hours in the academic field is preferred Extensive professional experience in a related field Minimum technology requirements must be met, those can be viewed at: https://www.trine.edu/online/student-support/technology.aspx Previous experience teaching online students at the university level Salary Salary is is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Adjunct faculty candidates are required to provide official transcripts during the\n                                    candidate selection process. Are you ready to join Trine? Complete an application for each academic field of interest.  Applications are being\n                                    accepted in the following academic fields: Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - English Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Psychology Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Philosophy Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Math Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Biology Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Business Administration Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Hybrid - Information Systems Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/undergraduate-adjunct-professor-math-detroit.aspx": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Math Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Math Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Math More in this Page Careers A Great Place to Work! Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Math Detroit, Michigan Summary Trine University invites applications for part-time adjunct positions in the following\n                                    academic fields: Math This adjunct faculty position is for online faculty who will travel to our Detroit,\n                                       Michigan location oncer per eight week term, per course (this is subject to change). Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to support program and enrollment growth.\n                                    Applications are active for one year from submission date. The Adjunct Faculty Role The University’s mission is to promote intellectual and personal development through\n                                    personally focused learning opportunities, preparing students to succeed, lead and\n                                    serve. Our faculty are responsible for ensuring students are successful in the online\n                                    classroom and are prepared for the complexities of today’s workplace. It is expected that adjunct faculty will: Actively engage students through frequent interaction and convey a genuine enthusiasm\n                                       for their learning. Provide thorough and constructive feedback, utilizing rubrics to effectively assess\n                                       learners’ work, while also acknowledging learner accomplishments. Demonstrate relevant and current subject-matter expertise and help students connect\n                                       concepts across their academic program. Work effectively with the TrineOnline team to seek continuous improvement for all\n                                       TrineOnline courses and programs. Adjunct Faculty Training All new faculty teaching online are required to successfully complete onboarding training\n                                    as a condition of hire. Required Education A master’s degree from an accredited institution of higher learning with a minimum\n                                       of 18 graduate credit hours in the academic field Extensive professional experience in a related field Minimum technology requirements must be met, those can be viewed at: https://www.trine.edu/online/student-support/technology.aspx Previous experience teaching online students at the university level Salary Salary is is based upon the number of credit hours taught and the number of students\n                                    registered for the class being taught. Adjunct faculty candidates are required to provide official transcripts during the\n                                    candidate selection process. Are you ready to join Trine? Trine University is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for employment\n                                    without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, disability, national origin, genetic\n                                    information, citizenship status, military status, or any other basis prohibited by\n                                    law, unless such basis constitutes a bona fide occupational qualification. Trine will\n                                    comply with its legal obligation to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified\n                                    individuals with disabilities and for religious beliefs. Take the Next Steps Apply Now Visit Request Info Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://careers.compass-usa.com/": {
      "title": "A FAMILY OF COMPANIES,A CAREER FOR LIFE",
      "description": "Compass Group Careers Sign In Current Employees Talent Community Careers\n                                    Home Why Compass? Benefits Awards Career Growth Recognition About US COI Sustainability Veterans Who we are Career Areas Operations Corporate Roles Students\n                                    & Grads Job Search Click to search Careers Home Why Compass? Benefits Awards Career Growth Recognition About Us COI Sustainability Veterans Who We Are Career Areas Operations Corporate Roles Students & Grads Sign In Job Search Your browser does not support the video tag. A FAMILY OF COMPANIES, A CAREER FOR LIFE I'm Looking For Position near Search WE’RE COMPASS GROUP But you might know us by a different name As the nation’s largest family of foodservice and facilities\n            services companies, you could make an impact anywhere — from college\n            quads and hospital dining rooms to ballparks, museums, school\n            cafeterias, corporate cafés, airport lounges, and senior living\n            communities. OUR FAMILY OF COMPANIES See your current employer? Then you’re already part of the team —\n            you should apply for your next career move here . MEET OLIVIA Our recruiting assistant, Olivia, can help you with your job\n              search, answer questions about working at Compass Group, guide you\n              through the application process, and even help schedule your\n              interview. You can click on the button to chat or you can text\n              \"Job\" to 75000. Chat with Olivia Invited to an interview You have been invited to a 30 min interview with Compass! Now Our stats 160 k+ NEW TEAM MEMBERS HIRED ANNUALLY 13,000 + NEW OPPORTUNITIES EVERY YEAR 28 + COMPANIES NATIONWIDE 13 M+ MEALS SERVED DAILY 1 B+ SQUARE FEET CLEANED DAILY 11 M+ HOSPITAL PATIENTS TRANSPORTED ANNUALLY 300 k+ ASSOCIATES IN THE U.S. AND CANADA 38 % OF OUR SALARIED TEAM MEMBERS ARE HIRED INTERNALLY Awards Our success didn’t happen overnight. We’ve earned the top spot in\n            our industry through decades of collaboration. Our awards say it\n            best. World’s Most Admired Company* Best Employers for Women Best Employers for Diversity Best Employers for New Grads Most Innovative Companies Ranked #1 out of 50 Compass in the news *Compass Group PLC, a Fortune 2023 & 2025 World's Most Admired\n            Company and a Time 2024 World's Best Company ** Number of years awards recieved. ABOUT US It takes a special team to deliver world-class hospitality and\n                  support services on a stage this big. Learn More WHY COMPASS? Benefits, career growth, recognition and more — there are so\n                  many reasons to choose a career at Compass Group. Learn More CAREER AREAS Build a great career in hospitality or support services, or\n                  join the team behind the scenes at our corporate headquarters. Learn More JOIN OUR TALENT COMMUNITY Stay up-to-date on our latest opportunities by signing up for job\n              alerts in our talent community. SIGN ME UP MEET US AT A HIRING EVENT Join us at one of our next hiring events, whether it’s virtual or\n              in-person. FIND AN EVENT NEAR YOU JOIN our FAMILY Your future is waiting. Let’s get started. Search Jobs Careers Home Hiring\n              Events Talent Community Search Jobs Compass-USA.com Current Employees Why Compass? Awards Benefits Career Growth Recognition About Us Inclusion and Belonging Sustainability Veterans Who We Are Career Areas Corporate Field Students & Grads Internships Accelerated Manager Program © 2025 Compass Group North America Applicants with Disabilities Code of Business Conduct Contact Us Employment Posters & Forms Equal Opportunity Employer Privacy Policy Privacy Requests Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://www.follett.com/careers": {
      "title": "Join theFollettteam",
      "description": "Careers - Follett Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us Campus Solutions RETAIL EXPERIENCES We support the entire academic journey, to help your students learn, thrive, and celebrate. Campus Store Virtual & Hybrid Stores Fan Shops ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Our focus is on providing students everything they need to succeed affordably. Access Programs Financial Aid Seamless Integrations Course Materials MERCHANDISE SOLUTIONS Our unmatched assortment helps you meet the needs of every customer. Apparel & Merchandise Cafés & Convenience Technology Campus Direct Sales Who We Help Students Academic Leaders Alumni & Development Faculty Campus Auxiliary Services Athletic Departments Fans Campus Technology Brand Partners Resources Campus Connections Blog Podcasts & Videos Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook About Us The Academic Journey Our Mission Meet Our Team Careers Press & Media Contact Us About Us About Us Careers We’re looking for people who are passionate about shaping the future of higher education. Find your fit in our full-time, part-time, and seasonal roles across retail, corporate, or warehouse settings in the US or Canada. Join the Follett team We are currently hiring for several full-time, part-time, and seasonal positions. Please click below for retail, corporate, and warehouse jobs in the US or Canada. Retail Jobs Connect directly with the campuses you love. Many of our retail team members are students or alumni from the campuses they serve, fostering a unique and personal link to the academic community. Opportunities range from temporary team members to team leads and store management. View Openings Corporate Jobs Join our corporate team to play a direct role in shaping the future of higher education. We’re pioneering new approaches, practices, and solutions that help campuses thrive. Be part of an organization that is dedicated to inspiring, enabling, and celebrating the academic journey. Opportunities extend across our headquarters and other office locations. View Openings Seasonal Jobs We’re on the lookout for seasonal team members to join our dynamic crew supporting campus stores, warehouses, and events. We offer weekly pay and flexible hours with opportunities in the US and Canada. Our partner NXTThing RPO helps coordinate seasonal hiring; we’re always looking for people to join the Follett team! View Openings Follett Corporation is an Equal Opportunity Employer Reasonable Accommodation We are an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment, without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status, or other characteristics protected by law. As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Follett is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to job applicants with disabilities. If you are interested in applying for employment and need assistance or an accommodation in the application process due to a disability, please contact us by email or phone. Email: Send request to follettaccomodations@follett.com Phone: Request assistance by calling 1.844.324.4748 (HR4U) For Hearing Impaired: Dial 7-1-1 or click on the accessibility icon We are here to answer your questions and provide assistance Monday to Friday, 7am-6pm Central Time, except national holidays. When contacting us, please provide your contact information, the job position or title, and state the nature of your accessibility issue. Notice on Recruiting Scams Thank you for your interest in Follett. We encourage you to explore job opportunities at Follett on our website, follett.com/careers . We caution you to be wary of internet, email and telephone scams in which fraudsters may try to take advantage of job seekers by pretending to represent Follett. We have been made aware of individuals and organizations falsely pretending to recruit on behalf of, or be affiliated with, Follett. Intended victims have been invited to participate in bogus interviews, asked to fill out fabricated employment applications and have even been issued fake offer letters, all with the ultimate goal of trying to entice victims to divulge sensitive personal information. These communications are fraudulent and do not originate from Follett nor are they associated with our recruitment process. We never ask job applicants for money. Follett will not send you a check (for immediate mobile deposit) to purchase equipment at any point in the recruitment process. Please note all seasonal hiring is done through our partner NXTThing RPO. To learn more about NXTTHING, visit: https://www.nxtthingrpo.com/ . How to Identify Recruiting Scams? Here are few things to watch for: Correspondence from the fraudsters are usually from free email accounts, like Yahoo!, Hotmail or Gmail. A Follett team member will not solicit candidates through a non-Follett email address or phone number. In addition, Follett does not utilize video chat rooms (e.g. Google Hangouts) to conduct interviews or contact potential candidates about a job opportunity via text messaging or instant messaging; The use of the English language, in written communication, is poor; Communications that are unsolicited or unexpected or are from an individual or website with which you are unfamiliar or whose domain name is inconsistent with that used by the actual business; Job opportunities and offers that appear “too good to be true”; Communications at the application phase requesting your social security number, national insurance number, date of birth, bank account information or other sensitive personal information; Insisting on urgency and that they are very interested in hiring you now; and, Requesting that you cash a check to purchase office equipment, or send money to Follett to purchase equipment. Follett has no responsibility for fraudulent job offers and advises interested applicants to follow the guidance provided above. If you believe you have been a victim of a recruiting scam, please: Contact your local law enforcement authorities and file a police report and provide them with all information you may have (email addresses, phone/fax details, etc., copies of emails/letters). Contact U.S. Department of Justice at www.stopfraud.gov Please email us at recruitingfraud@follett.com , and use the term “fraudulent job offer” in the subject/re box. Follett is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. © 2023 FOLLETT CORPORATION Learn more about Follett’s mission, services, and goals. Connect with us Need more information? CONTACT FOLLETT CAMPUS SOLUTIONS Campus Store Course Materials Access Programs Apparel & Merchandise Fan Shops Virtual & Hybrid Stores Technology ABOUT US Our Mission The Academic Journey Meet Our Team Press & Media Careers Brand Partnerships Policies CUSTOMER SUPPORT Customer Support Center Contact Us Find Your Campus Store RESOURCES Podcasts & Videos Campus Connections Blog Webinars & Events Virtual Lookbook Terms of Use Privacy Policy Cookies Copyright © 2026 Follett Corporation | 3 Westbrook Corporate Center, Westchester, IL 60154"
    },
    "https://www.trine.edu/human-resources/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Trine University Go to site search Go to main navigation Go to main content Search Go Academics Majors and Degrees Online Programs Dual Enrollment Academic Opportunities Career Preparation Study Abroad Centers Schools Academic Support & Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Libraries Accreditation Become a Student How to Apply Admission Counselors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid & Scholarships Visit Trine Transfer Resources Request Information Admitted Students Lifetime Guarantee Life at Trine Our Campus Campus Map Housing & Res Life Dining Athletics Upcoming Events Clubs & Organizations Music & Performing Arts Student Support Office of Student Affairs Financial Aid International Student Resources Student Support and Wellness Services Safety TrineOnline Info For Parents & Families Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Employers International Students About Trine News Give Athletics Alumni International Apply Visit Request Info Home Office of Human Resources Careers Careers More in this Page Office of Human Resources A Great Place to Work! Trine is always on the lookout for talented individuals. Welcome to Trine University's Recruitment Page! We’re thrilled that you’re considering joining our team. At Trine, we’re passionate\n                                    about creating a dynamic work environment where innovation thrives, and every individual\n                                    has the opportunity to grow, collaborate, and make an impact. As one of the largest\n                                    employers in Steuben County, Trine prides itself on its employee retention, outstanding\n                                    benefits, creative work environment, and its contribution to the community. Whether you’re just starting your career or bringing years of experience, we’re always\n                                    on the lookout for talented, motivated people who share our values and vision. Explore\n                                    our current job openings and discover how you can be a part of something truly exciting. Staff Positions (Angola Campus) Administrative Assistant Assistant Figure and Synchronized Skating Coach Campus Safety Officer Director of Development Director of Dual Enrollment Financial Aid Counselor Housekeeper Human Resource Specialist Instructional Support Assistant Maintenance/Building Mechanic Part-time Academic Coach Part-time Campus Safety Officer Part-time CDL Driver Part-time Weekend Housekeeper Student Success Representative Staff Positions (Education Centers) Help Desk Specialist (Fort Wayne, Indiana) International Services Advisor (Reston, Virginia) International Services Processor (Detroit, Michigan) Part-time Surgical Technologist Clinical & Lab Supervisor (Fort Wayne, Indiana) Practical Training Processor (Phoenix, Arizona) Student Success Representative (Detroit, Michigan) Faculty Positions (Angola Campus) Assistant/Associate Professor - Civil Engineering (Transportation) Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical or Chemical Engineering Adjunct Professor - Accounting Adjunct Professor - Applied Music Adjunct Professor - Business Adjunct Professor - Chemistry Adjunct Professor - Criminal Justice Adjunct Professor - Education Adjunct Professor - English Adjunct Professor - Forensic Science Adjunct Professor - Humanities and Communication Adjunct Professor - Jazz/Show Choir Ensemble Adjunct Professor - Marketing Adjunct Professor - Music & Athletic Band Adjunct Professor - Nursing Adjunct Professor - Physics Adjunct Professor - Psychology Faculty Positions (Education Centers) Assistant / Associate Professor - Physical Therapy Part-time Assistant Professor/PA Educator - (Fort Wayne, Indiana) Adjunct Positions (Education Centers/TrineOnline) Adjunct Professor - Nursing (Fort Wayne, Indiana) Physician Assistant - Adjunct Professor (Fort Wayne, Indiana) Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid (Phoenix, Arizona) Doctoral Adjunct Professor - Information Technology - Hybrid (Reston, Virginia) Graduate Adjunct Professor Positions - Hybrid (Reston, Virginia) Graduate Adjunct Professor Positions - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Business Analytics - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Business Analytics - Hybrid (Phoenix, Arizona) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Business Analytics - Hybrid (Reston, Virginia) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Information Studies - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Information Studies - Hybrid (Phoenix, Arizona) Graduate Adjunct Professor Positions - Hybrid (Phoenix, Arizona) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Statistics - Hybrid (Phoenix, Arizona) Graduate Adjunct Professor - Statistics - Hybrid (Reston, Virginia) Undergraduate Adjunct Professor Positions - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Undergraduate Adjunct Professor - Math - Hybrid (Detroit, Michigan) Bon Appetit (On-Site Food Service) View all open positions Follett (On-Site Bookstore) View all open positions Contact Information Human Resources Trine University 1 University Avenue Angola, Indiana 46703-1764 260.665.4847 260.665.4991 260.665.4828 Fax Note: All candidates must provide proof of eligibility to work in the United States and\n                                    official transcripts at the time of employment. Please supply letter of interest,\n                                    resume and contact information for three professional references. As an equal opportunity employer, Trine University does not discriminate in its employment\n                                    decisions on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, pregnancy,\n                                    childbirth and related conditions, lactation status, gender identity, sexual orientation,\n                                    age, disability, veteran or military status, genetic information, ancestry or any\n                                    other protected status as required by law. Take the Next Steps learn more about trine Visit Request Info cost & affordability Tuition Financial Aid apply Apply Now Contact information for Trine University 260.665.4100 800.347.4878 One University Avenue Angola, IN 46703 Helpful Links Employment Contact Us Maps & Directions Logins MyPortal Moodle Webmail Affiliates TrineOnline Trine Innovation 1 Education One Zollner Golf Course T. Furth Center for Performing Arts Trine Broadcasting Network Copyright © 2026 Trine University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy Title IX Student Right to Know Social Media Links Twitter Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube SmugMug ©"
    },
    "https://a.cms.omniupdate.com/11/?skin=oucampus&account=trine&site=www-2023&action=de&path=/human-resources/careers/index.pcf": {
